{"task_id": "Mbpp/794", "original_task_id": 794, "entry_point": "text_starta_endb", "prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an 'a' followed by anything, ending in 'b'.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef text_starta_endb(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an 'a' followed by anything, ending in 'b'.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef text_starta_endb(text):\r\n        patterns = 'a.*?b$'\r\n        if re.search(patterns,  text):\r\n                return 'Found a match!'\r\n        else:\r\n                return('Not matched!')", "tests": "assert text_starta_endb(\"aabbbb\")==('Found a match!')\nassert text_starta_endb(\"aabAbbbc\")==('Not matched!')\nassert text_starta_endb(\"accddbbjjj\")==('Not matched!')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/850", "original_task_id": 850, "entry_point": "is_triangleexists", "prompt": "Write a function to check if a triangle of positive area is possible with the given angles.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_triangleexists(a, b, c):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if a triangle of positive area is possible with the given angles.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_triangleexists(a,b,c): \r\n    if(a != 0 and b != 0 and c != 0 and (a + b + c)== 180): \r\n        if((a + b)>= c or (b + c)>= a or (a + c)>= b): \r\n            return True \r\n        else:\r\n            return False\r\n    else:\r\n        return False", "tests": "assert is_triangleexists(50,60,70)==True\nassert is_triangleexists(90,45,45)==True\nassert is_triangleexists(150,30,70)==False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/693", "original_task_id": 693, "entry_point": "remove_multiple_spaces", "prompt": "Write a function to remove multiple spaces in a string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_multiple_spaces(text1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove multiple spaces in a string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef remove_multiple_spaces(text1):\r\n  return (re.sub(' +',' ',text1))", "tests": "assert remove_multiple_spaces('Google      Assistant') == 'Google Assistant'\nassert remove_multiple_spaces('Quad      Core') == 'Quad Core'\nassert remove_multiple_spaces('ChromeCast      Built-in') == 'ChromeCast Built-in'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/702", "original_task_id": 702, "entry_point": "removals", "prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum number of elements that should be removed such that amax-amin<=k.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef removals(arr, n, k):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum number of elements that should be removed such that amax-amin<=k.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_ind(key, i, n, \r\n\t\t\tk, arr):\r\n\tind = -1\r\n\tstart = i + 1\r\n\tend = n - 1;\r\n\twhile (start < end):\r\n\t\tmid = int(start +\r\n\t\t\t\t(end - start) / 2)\r\n\t\tif (arr[mid] - key <= k):\r\n\t\t\tind = mid\r\n\t\t\tstart = mid + 1\r\n\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\tend = mid\r\n\treturn ind\r\ndef removals(arr, n, k):\r\n\tans = n - 1\r\n\tarr.sort()\r\n\tfor i in range(0, n):\r\n\t\tj = find_ind(arr[i], i, \r\n\t\t\t\t\tn, k, arr)\r\n\t\tif (j != -1):\r\n\t\t\tans = min(ans, n -\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t(j - i + 1))\r\n\treturn ans", "tests": "assert removals([1, 3, 4, 9, 10,11, 12, 17, 20], 9, 4) == 5\nassert removals([1, 5, 6, 2, 8], 5, 2) == 3\nassert removals([1, 2, 3 ,4, 5, 6], 6, 3) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/937", "original_task_id": 937, "entry_point": "max_char", "prompt": "Write a function to count the most common character in a given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_char(str1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to count the most common character in a given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import Counter \r\ndef max_char(str1):\r\n    temp = Counter(str1) \r\n    max_char = max(temp, key = temp.get)\r\n    return max_char", "tests": "assert max_char(\"hello world\")==('l')\nassert max_char(\"hello \")==('l')\nassert max_char(\"python pr\")==('p')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
