{"task_id": "Mbpp/747", "original_task_id": 747, "entry_point": "lcs_of_three", "prompt": "Write a function to find the longest common subsequence for the given three string sequence.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef lcs_of_three(X, Y, Z, m, n, o):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the longest common subsequence for the given three string sequence.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def lcs_of_three(X, Y, Z, m, n, o): \r\n\tL = [[[0 for i in range(o+1)] for j in range(n+1)] \r\n\t\tfor k in range(m+1)] \r\n\tfor i in range(m+1): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(n+1): \r\n\t\t\tfor k in range(o+1): \r\n\t\t\t\tif (i == 0 or j == 0 or k == 0): \r\n\t\t\t\t\tL[i][j][k] = 0\r\n\t\t\t\telif (X[i-1] == Y[j-1] and\r\n\t\t\t\t\tX[i-1] == Z[k-1]): \r\n\t\t\t\t\tL[i][j][k] = L[i-1][j-1][k-1] + 1\r\n\t\t\t\telse: \r\n\t\t\t\t\tL[i][j][k] = max(max(L[i-1][j][k], \r\n\t\t\t\t\tL[i][j-1][k]), \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tL[i][j][k-1]) \r\n\treturn L[m][n][o]", "tests": "assert lcs_of_three('AGGT12', '12TXAYB', '12XBA', 6, 7, 5) == 2\nassert lcs_of_three('Reels', 'Reelsfor', 'ReelsforReels', 5, 8, 13) == 5 \nassert lcs_of_three('abcd1e2', 'bc12ea', 'bd1ea', 7, 6, 5) == 3", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "validation", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
